The sanctioned place for a state change in a declarative body, pinned on all
three targets. Written as bare statements of the view body -- `n = 5`, `n++`,
`flag!!` -- the same writes checked clean and then diverged: fyne put
`m.n = 5` in its builder while bubbletea and html discarded it, and
`sngl generate` exited 0 either way. The checker now refuses all four kinds
there, so what is left to pin is where they go instead: an effect's @mount,
which runs once, and a handler, which runs on the event.

Read the three builders below and none of them carries a write: bubbletea's
View(), the Compose Column and html's tree are the tree alone, and every
mutation is in __effect0_mount, the DisposableEffect or the click handler.

There is deliberately no `deny` line for it: nothing moves a write out of an
effect, so the pattern would match in no state at all, which is the vacuous
kind.

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

var n = 0
var flag = false

component main node {
    effect(@mount {
        n = 5
        n++
    })

    button(text="flip", @click {
        flag!!
        n = n + 1
    })
    text(value="{n} {flag}")
}

window {
    main
}
